{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"advisory":[{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Confirm the intended contract: should parsed_python_files raise on unparseable/unreadable in-repo files (hard-fail the first scanner) or preserve the per-oracle skip semantics the migrated try/except blocks provided?","criteria":["error-handling","regression"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/_tree_scan.py:44-46 `for path in sorted(root.rglob(\"*.py\")): source = path.read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\"); modules.append(ParsedModule(path, source, ast.parse(source, filename=str(path))))` — no exception handling","test_gate_context_seam.py dropped `try: tree = ast.parse(...) except SyntaxError: # pragma: no cover - not our concern here / continue`","test_single_definition_helpers.py dropped `except SyntaxError: # pragma: no cover - a syntactically broken file is CI's problem / continue`","test_review_discovery_architecture.py previously used `read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")` and `except SyntaxError: continue`; now strict utf-8 with no skip","test_rich_reemit_state.py dropped `except SyntaxError: # pragma: no cover — a parse failure is its own gate's problem / continue`"],"finding":"parsed_python_files() reads with strict utf-8 and bare ast.parse (no try/except), so migrated oracles that previously caught (SyntaxError, OSError) and skipped now hard-fail: a single unparseable or non-utf-8 .py under the root raises out of the shared scanner and fails whichever test first materializes that root's cache entry, not the oracle that 'owns' the check.","id":"0","impact":0.3,"location":"tests/_tree_scan.py:42","norm_id":"nb3f93502b8f8e4d8","priority":0.3,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":1.0,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"yes","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"system","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":false,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":true,"implicit_coupling":true,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.5,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Restore the generator-symmetric skip semantics in test_gen_env_registry.py or verify the generator's census also hard-fails on the same files so both sides stay aligned.","criteria":["error-handling","regression","maintainability"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["removed block per diff: `except (SyntaxError, OSError): # Same skip set as the generator's own census... an unreadable file must drop out of BOTH sides, or the oracle reports a stale row the generator would never raise on. / continue`","new code tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py:254-255 `for module in parsed_python_files(root): tree = module.tree` — no skip; parsed_python_files raises on unreadable/unparseable"],"finding":"test_gen_env_registry.py removed a skip guard whose in-code comment documented it as load-bearing: the census must drop the SAME unreadable/unparseable files as the generator's own census, or it reports a stale row the generator would never raise on. Migrating to parsed_python_files (which raises instead of skipping) silently breaks that documented symmetry.","id":"1","impact":0.27,"location":"tests/unit/test_gen_env_registry.py:254","norm_id":"n592fc1fc134db620","priority":0.2314,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded":false,"churn90":0,"contract_drift":true,"data_loss_without_recovery":false,"dead_code":false,"debt_impact":"medium","escapes_automation":true,"forbids_contract_allowed_state":false,"hard_to_reverse_surface":false,"hidden_invariant":true,"implicit_coupling":false,"likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reachable_path_without_automated_coverage":false,"removed_public_symbol":false,"reversibility":"easy","safety_net_removal_without_replacement":false,"security_bypass_not_enforced_elsewhere":false,"silent_failure":false,"silent_wrong_feeding_a_decision":false,"trigger_likelihood":"rare","unversioned_published_contract_break":false,"version_signal_present":false}}},{"agreement":1,"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Avoid mutating cached AST nodes in _trees_with_parents (build a side-table parents dict keyed by node identity, as test_subcall_class_selection._ast_index already does) rather than writing child.parent onto shared trees.","criteria":["maintainability","concurrency"],"decision":"advisory","evidence":["tests/unit/test_compute_validity_callers.py:16-21 `for module in parsed_python_files(root): tree = module.tree; for parent in ast.walk(tree): for child in ast.iter_child_nodes(parent): child.parent = parent`","tests/_tree_scan.py:33 `@functools.cache` — same ParsedModule/tree objects are returned on every call with the same root","tests/_tree_scan.py:24 ParsedModule uses __slots__ but ast.AST nodes do not, so `.parent` assignment mutates the shared tree in place"],"finding":"test_compute_validity_callers._trees_with_parents mutates the shared, cached AST nodes returned by parsed_python_files (child.parent = parent). Because the functools.cache aliases the same ast.AST objects to every test scanning src/rebar in a worker, this writes onto process-global shared state that other oracles also walk.","id":"2","impact":0.3,"location":"tests/unit/test_compute_validity_callers.py:16","norm_id":"n1b817d7d88fd3cd1","priority":0.2571,"reason":"default-advisory","scenarios":[],"severity":"minor","suggested_fix":"Replace the in-place `child.parent = parent` mutation with a local `parents: dict[ast.AST, ast.AST]` mapping built per call, matching the non-mutating pattern in test_subcall_class_selection._ast_index.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.8571,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"na","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"no","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"yes","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"yes","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"yes","path_reachable":"yes","respects_artifact_altitude":"na","severity_claim_justified":"yes"},"severity_attributes":{"blast_radius":"module","capability_degraded